take the Advance SP shell off a stretched picture

This restores what stretching did before the rebase onto upstream f4b7bc3,
and it changes how Game Boy and Game Boy Color carts look in that mode.

L1 stretches a Game Boy picture until it fills the panel's height, and
App::shown_game_bezel already drops a console's own bezel while it is
stretched. f4b7bc3 added a second kind of frame that has no such rule: when
the AGS-102 Advance SP shell is picked, which is the default for every
console on a 4:3 panel, draw_sp_strip lays the shell's lettering strip over
the lower part of the game, and the compositor pins the picture to the top
of the panel. With a picture that already fills the height, the strip lands
on game rows, and it did so on every launch because the mode is remembered
per cart.

sp_frame() is the one question both of those ask, so it answers false while
the picture is stretched, the same rule shown_game_bezel applies.

diff --git a/crates/slot/src/app.rs b/crates/slot/src/app.rs
--- a/crates/slot/src/app.rs
+++ b/crates/slot/src/app.rs
@@ -1119,6 +1119,9 @@
     }
 
     pub fn sp_frame(&self) -> bool {
+        if self.video_mode == VideoMode::Stretch {
+            return false;
+        }
         self.resolved_bezel(self.playing_platform()) == BezelPick::Ags102
     }
 
diff --git a/crates/slot/tests/app.rs b/crates/slot/tests/app.rs
--- a/crates/slot/tests/app.rs
+++ b/crates/slot/tests/app.rs
@@ -1942,6 +1942,26 @@
             }
         );
     }
+}
+
+#[test]
+fn stretching_a_game_boy_takes_the_advance_sp_shell_off() {
+    let d = common::tmp_root_with_gb_carts(&["Tetris"]);
+    let mut s = session_playing(d.path());
+    s.app_mut().set_panel((640, 480));
+    assert!(
+        s.app().sp_frame(),
+        "the shell is the default on a 4:3 panel"
+    );
+    s.feed([RawEvent::Down(Btn::L1)], 100);
+    s.feed([RawEvent::Up(Btn::L1)], 120);
+    assert!(
+        !s.app().sp_frame(),
+        "the shell's strip would sit over a picture that fills the height"
+    );
+    s.feed([RawEvent::Down(Btn::R1)], 140);
+    s.feed([RawEvent::Up(Btn::R1)], 160);
+    assert!(s.app().sp_frame());
 }
 
 #[test]
